{"assets":["/statement-assets/5ae50b316b1c421933dacfcf924e764506ab3ef856fe84451a5c7732c6d549b0.png","/statement-assets/fa802fffcd77185c1e1f86f6ae34abacead1e14c0dfc29bb5fcac7b684092278.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"335","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. More Reclamation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a far away land, there are two cities near a river. One day, the cities decide that they have too little space and would like to reclaim some of the river area into land."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The river area can be represented by a grid with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" rows and exactly two columns — each cell represents a rectangular area. The rows are numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" from top to bottom, while the columns are numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initially, all of the cells are occupied by the river. The plan is to turn some of those cells into land one by one, with the cities alternately choosing a cell to reclaim, and continuing until no more cells can be reclaimed."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, the river is also used as a major trade route. The cities need to make sure that ships will still be able to sail from one end of the river to the other. More formally, if a cell "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(r, c)"},{"kind":"text","text":" has been reclaimed, it is not allowed to reclaim any of the cells "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(r - 1, 3 - c)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(r, 3 - c)"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(r + 1, 3 - c)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The cities are not on friendly terms, and each city wants to be the last city to reclaim a cell (they don't care about how many cells they reclaim, just who reclaims a cell last). The cities have already reclaimed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" cells. Your job is to determine which city will be the last to reclaim a cell, assuming both choose cells optimally from current moment."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line consists of two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"r"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ r ≤ 100, 0 ≤ n ≤ r"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines follow, describing the cells that were already reclaimed. Each line consists of two integers: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ri ≤ r, 1 ≤ ci ≤ 2"},{"kind":"text","text":"), which represent the cell located at row "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":" and column "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ci"},{"kind":"text","text":". All of the lines describing the cells will be distinct, and the reclaimed cells will not violate the constraints above."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"WIN"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the city whose turn it is to choose a cell can guarantee that they will be the last to choose a cell. Otherwise print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"LOSE"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 1\n1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"WIN\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12 2\n4 1\n8 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"WIN\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 1\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"LOSE\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, there are 3 possible cells for the first city to reclaim: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(3, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":", or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(3, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The first two possibilities both lose, as they leave exactly one cell for the other city."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/5ae50b316b1c421933dacfcf924e764506ab3ef856fe84451a5c7732c6d549b0.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, reclaiming the cell at "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(3, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":" leaves no more cells that can be reclaimed, and therefore the first city wins."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/fa802fffcd77185c1e1f86f6ae34abacead1e14c0dfc29bb5fcac7b684092278.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, there are no cells that can be reclaimed."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"335C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/335/problem/C"}